          "general_description": "ARC-AGI-2 evaluates AI completion of coloured-grid problems. Worked input/output examples define an unstated transformation that the system must apply to new inputs. The released materials include 1,000 development problems and public, semi-private and private evaluation sets of 120 problems each. Developers used human puzzle-solving results and internal review to select tasks and match the evaluation sets for human difficulty. Each new input permits two attempts, with credit requiring an exact output grid. The inspected scorer averages input-level success within each problem and then averages problem scores. Verified ARC Prize evaluations specify settings and spending limits and use one run. Public data, software and marking tests permit inspection; hidden materials have controlled access. No distinct skill scales or AI reference norms are supplied. The creators associate the benchmark with reasoning and broader intelligence, while the supplied empirical account concerns two-dimensional grid tasks."
        },
        "part_B": {
